            text: "It is the pressure exerted by water sitting in saturated soil against the outside of your foundation walls and underneath the floor slab. Water weighs about 62 pounds per cubic foot, so every foot of water above a point adds roughly 0.43 psi. When the soil around a basement is saturated, that pressure pushes water through every crack, joint and pore it can find.",
